      "message": "To elaborate on the example I provided in the description a bit more:\n\nThread 1 (main thread):\n- future \u003d MapAsync(..., [\u0026]callback)\n- loop WaitAny(future, 0)\n\nThread 2 (Metal thread):\n- Metal thread notifies that the serial is ready\n- Calls |EnsureComplete| and sets `mCompleted \u003d true`\n\nThread 1:\n- WaitAny checks and sees that event is ready\n- WaitImpl calls |EnsureComplete|, sees `mCompleted` is already true so continues, returning Success for the WaitAny call\n- Test continues and starts tearing down destroying things that were captured in the callback scope.\n\nThread 2:\n- Finally starts running the |Complete| call which calls the callback, but test has already destroyed everything in the capture scope so we crash.\n\n\nBy using a lock instead of the atomic, we guarantee that if WaitAny sees the event is ready and calls |EnsureComplete| on it, that the callback will have fully ran before we return Success from WaitAny.",
